WEBVTT

00:00.375 --> 00:05.625
SafeVantage: Vantage-Aware Memory for Reliable Embodied Decisions.

00:13.438 --> 00:19.562
Is there a paper towel in the room? A first observation supplies partial evidence.

00:20.400 --> 00:31.600
SafeVantage links each claim to its source observations, camera poses, and estimated target location.

00:32.406 --> 00:38.094
Candidate geometry helps predict whether a viewpoint can reveal the target.

00:38.906 --> 00:44.594
View selection seeks expected reduction in decision loss while accounting for travel and distinct corroboration.

00:45.446 --> 00:53.482
Inspect the surrounding views.

00:53.929 --> 01:03.750
Move to a distinct viewpoint. Robot motion and the moving camera are illustrated.

01:04.196 --> 01:09.554
Retain the corroborating recorded observation.

01:10.385 --> 01:19.615
Supporting views come from distinct camera positions and provide consistent target estimates.

01:20.385 --> 01:29.615
A calibrated head combines viewpoint support, geometric agreement, and search coverage to return Yes, No, or Abstain.

01:30.429 --> 01:41.571
The manuscript evaluates 232 unseen ProcTHOR houses and 7,424 paired episodes per method and action budget.

01:42.375 --> 01:47.625
SafeVantage. safevantage.github.io
